No, that kind of vault - which for some reason has been dubbed a
"Magic Memory Vault" by the game's fans - can occur on ANY normal
dungeon level with rooms and corridors. (Note: Some levels are not
considered "normal" for this purpose, including levels of the Quest or
levels with more than two staircases, and of course you cannot get one
in a Maze level such as the normal dungeon below Medusa, or in
Gehennom.)

What it is, essentially, is a 2x2 room surrounded by walls with a
large pile of gold on each of the four squares, and no doors in any of
the walls. You can get into it by teleporting or by digging, and you
can get out of it by teleporting or by digging or by following the
guard when he arrives (this is the only way out if you have no means
of teleport and did not arrive by digging through the wall.)

Sometimes, of course, a dwarf or rock mole will tunnel through the
wall for you, and most likely pick up the gold too. The guard will
only arrive if you are actually standing on one of the vault's
squares, so if you get the gold and teleport or dig your way out,
you've robbed the bank successfully.

At any level below dungeon level 10, if there is one of these vaults
on the level, there is a chance that it will contain a portal to the
legendary Fort Ludios, home of masses of wealth, masses of soldiers,
several dragons, and the richest man of legendary history - Croesus of
Lydia, who famously found that all his legendary wealth could not buy
him either happiness or military success. (Consulting an oracle before
he went to war, he received the advice that "A great empire will be
defeated". The empire in question turned out to be his own.)

In any Magic Memory vault, if the guard comes to ask what you're doing
there and who you are, there is ONE false name you can give, which
will make him go away. (Which is okay if you have another way out,
such as a means of digging or teleporting, and not good if you do not
have another way out.) Otherwise you will have to either fight him or
drop ALL the gold you are carrying in the vault and follow him out.

